      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Apologies for the goblin misstep. Let's get straight to the logistics then. If you're dropping off your cases at your Tokyo hotel on a Monday morning, it's a bit like setting out on a quest with a tight schedule. To ensure your cases arrive by Tuesday afternoon in Osaka, you would typically need to account for the time it takes for Yamato to pick up, transport, and deliver your luggage.\n\nYamato's service can vary, but generally, they aim to have your luggage delivered within 24 hours of pickup. So, if you drop off your cases on Monday, they should be on their way to Osaka by Tuesday morning. However, to be on the safe side and avoid any unexpected delays, it's wise to give them a few extra hours. A good rule of thumb would be to drop off your luggage by early afternoon on Monday, which should give Yamato enough time to handle any unforeseen circumstances and still have your cases waiting for you by Tuesday afternoon.\n\nAs for labeling, it's crucial to ensure your luggage doesn't get lost in the shuffle. Label each case clearly with your name, the destination (Osaka), and the date. You might also want to include your contact information in case there's any confusion. This is akin to",
